From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:32:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: An ACPI node for the M.2 Wi-Fi card

At every boot Linux prints "ACPI: \: failed to evaluate _DSM
2c176672-0b22-294b-814f-75e4dd26b5fd" twice: iwlwifi asks the product
reset _DSM (7266172C-220B-4B29-814F-75E4DD26B5FD) of the ACPI node of
the card, which has none behind root port 6, and the NULL handle fails
with AE_BAD_PARAMETER. Declare the card, _ADR 0, with no methods: a
missing _DSM is AE_NOT_FOUND, which acpi_evaluate_dsm() does not
report. No _PRW, as before: the wake of the card stays the OS's.

TEST=acpiexec with the DSDT of an M920x and this scope: the device is
\_SB.PCI0.RP06.WIFI with _ADR 0. The warning in the hardware test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/dsdt.asl | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/dsdt.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/dsdt.asl
index 777df2d431..a4dec07c22 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/dsdt.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/dsdt.asl
@@ -21,6 +21,19 @@ DefinitionBlock(
 		#include <soc/intel/cannonlake/acpi/southbridge.asl>
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The M.2 Wi-Fi card behind root port 6, with no method: iwlwifi asks
+	 * its _DSM for the product reset and, without an ACPI node for the card,
+	 * warns at every boot (AE_BAD_PARAMETER); a missing method is quiet.
+	 */
+	Scope (\_SB.PCI0.RP06)
+	{
+		Device (WIFI)
+		{
+			Name (_ADR, 0)
+		}
+	}
+
 	/* What macOS looks for on this desktop, under macOS only */
 	#include "acpi/macos.asl"
 
